                  %div
                    %p
                      %a{:href => "/nlab/edit/differential+cohomology+-+contents"} Edit this sidebar
          %h1#contents Contents
          .maruku_toc
            %ul
              %li
                %a{:href => "#idea"} Idea
              %li
                %a{:href => "#experimental_evidence"} Experimental evidence
              %li
                %a{:href => "#CriticalDiscussionOfTheLiterature"} Critical discussion of the literature
              %li
                %a{:href => "#related_concepts"} Related concepts
              %li
                %a{:href => "#References"} References
              %ul
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#general"} General
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#relation_to_skyrmions_calorons_monopoles"} Relation to skyrmions, calorons, monopoles
          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            In
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/QCD"} QCD
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/instanton"} instanton
            configurations of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+field"} gauge field
            control the experimentally observed
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vacuum"} vacuum
            structure of the theory.
          %p
            One considers QCD on a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Minkowski+spacetime"} Minkowski spacetime
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Wick+rotation"} Wick rotated
            to a Euclidean
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mn 4
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^4
            and assumes the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+strength"} field strength
            to
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vanish+at+infinity"} vanish at infinity
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi SU
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 3
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SU(3)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+connections"} principal connections
            on the 4-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sphere"} sphere
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 4
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^4
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/second+Chern+class"} second Chern class
            of the underlying
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+SU%283%29-bundle"} principal SU(3)-bundle
            is called the
            = succeed "-number" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yang-Mills+instanton"} Yang-Mills instanton
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vacuum"} vacuum
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/QCD"} QCD
            is some
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superposition"} superposition
            of gauge fields in various instanton number sectors.
          %p
            In particular the
            %strong instanton liquid model
            in QCD assumes that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vacuum"} vacuum
            (ground state of QCD) is populated by instanton field configurations of average radius
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mn 3
                  %mi fm
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1/3 fm
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/femtometres"}> femtometres
            ) with a density of 1 such instanton per
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi fm
                      %mn 4
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} fm^4
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#SchaeferShuryak"} Schaefer-Shuryak
          %p
            This instanton sea model suffers however from infrared divergencies that either require a finite-volume cutoff or appeal to other effects (e.g.
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#Witten98"} Witten 98
          %p
            But
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lattice+gauge+field+theory"} lattice gauge field theory
            simulations demonstrate numerically that the QCD vacuum is filled with instantons (e.g.
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#Gruber13"} Gruber 13, esp. sections 5 and 7
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#Schaefer02"} Schaefer 02
          %p
            The
            %em Witten-Veneziano formula
            (
            %a{:href => "#Witten79"}> Witten 79
            ,
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#Veneziano79"} Veneziano 79
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi η
                    %mo ′
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta'
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/particle"} particle
            in the limiting case that the gauge group is
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi SU
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi N
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SU(N)
            for
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi N
                    %mo →
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N \to \infty
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi N
                  %mo =
                  %mn 3
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N = 3
            includes (
            %a{:href => "#Creutz11"}> Creutz 11
            ).
          %h2#experimental_evidence Experimental evidence
          %p An instanton vacuum is argued to account for
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                formation of the gluon condensate (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mikhail+Shifman"}> Mikhail Shifman
                ,
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Arkady+Vainshtein"} Arkady Vainshtein
                and
                = succeed "," do
                  %span.newWikiWord
                    Vladimir Zakharov
                    %a{:href => "/nlab/new/Vladimir+Zakharov"} ?
            %li
              %p
                spontaneous
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chiral+symmetry+breaking"} chiral symmetry breaking
                (
                %a{:href => "#Diakonov96"}> Diakonov 96
                )
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/baryogenesis"} baryogenesis
                in the early universe by inducing baryon number non-conservation
          %h2#CriticalDiscussionOfTheLiterature Critical discussion of the literature
          %p
            In the physics literature a style of discussion of instantons is wide-spread where the motivation of the formulas considered is dubious. In these references (for instance
            %a{:href => "#SchaeferShuryak"} Schaefer-Shuryak 96
            and
            %a{:href => "#Forkel"} Forkel 00
            and many more) it is said that
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                a YM field of minimal energy, hence of vanishing
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+strength"} field strength
                is one that is pure gauge;
            %li
              %p
                that therefore on a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Minkowski+spacetime"} Minkowski spacetime
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mn 4
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^4
                in
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/temporal+gauge"} temporal gauge
                and assuming fields are
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vanishing+at+infinity"} vanishing at infinity
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connection+on+a+bundle"} connection
                1-forms on
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi S
                        %mn 3
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^3
                of the form
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi U
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mn 1
                      %mi d
                      %mi U
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U^{-1} d U
                for
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %msup
                        %mi S
                        %mn 3
                      %mo →
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U \colon S^3 \to G
                a smooth function, and
            %li
              %p
                that therefore equivalence classes of such fields are given by
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy"} homotopy
                classes of maps
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi S
                          %mn 3
                        %mo →
                        %mi G
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^3 \to G
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+group"} homotopy group
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi π
                          %mn 3
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi G
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_3(G)
          %p These points are not really correct, even though the conclusion about the classification of instanton sectors turns out to be right.
          %p
            The correct statement is that winding-number sectors/instanton sectors are equivalence classes of
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+bundles"} principal bundles
            on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/one-point+compactification"} one-point compactification
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 4
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^4
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Minkowski+spacetime"} Minkowski spacetime
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mn 4
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^4
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 3
                    %mo →
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^3 \to G
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 3
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^3
            regarded as the “equator” of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 4
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^4
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#Nakahara"} Nakahara
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#Witten85"} Witten 85
          %p Before we come to this, first notice the problems with the above items from the standard physics reviews:
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+field"} Gauge fields
                with vanishing
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+strength"} field strength
                are
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flat+connections"} flat connections
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group"} group
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homomorphisms"} homomorphisms
                from the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fundamental+group"} fundamental group
                of the given
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/space"} space
                or
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spacetime"} spacetime
                to the
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+group"} gauge group
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fundamental+group"} fundamental group
                is trivial. Of course this is the case on
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^n
                and
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi S
                          %mi n
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^n
            %li
              %p
                Flat connection on
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi S
                        %mn 3
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^3
                are not classified by homotopy classes of maps
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi S
                          %mn 3
                        %mo →
                        %mi G
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^3 \to G
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi π
                        %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msup
                        %mi S
                        %mn 3
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_1(S^3)
                is the trivial group, there is only the trivial such flat connection. This is actually manifest in the formula for such connections which is preferred in these references, which is “
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi U
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mn 1
                      %mi d
                      %mi U
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U^{-1} d U
                ” with
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %msup
                        %mi S
                        %mn 3
                      %mo →
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U \colon S^3 \to G
                a gauge transformation. That formula exhibits precisely the trivial gauge connection
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi d
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d
                as gauge equivalent to
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi U
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                            %mn 1
                        %mi d
                        %mi U
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U^{-1} d U
          %p
            What would give the intended classification is if one considered connections of the form
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi U
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                  %mi d
                  %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U^{-1} d U
            only modulo those gauge transformations
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi h
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 3
                  %mo →
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h \colon S^3 \to G
            which can be smoothly extended to maps
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi D
                      %mn 4
                    %mo →
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D^4 \to G
            = succeed "-principal" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
          %p
            And this brings us to the correct mathematical interpretation of instantons, as in (
            %a{:href => "#Nakahara"}> Nakahara
            ) and similar:
          %p
            We are looking for gauge field configurations on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mn 4
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^4
            that have
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+strength"} field strength
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vanishing+at+infinity"} vanishing at infinity
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+connections"} principal connections
            on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/one-point+compactification"} one-point compactification
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 4
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^4
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mn 4
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^4
            such that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/curvature"} curvature
            2-form vanishes at one “pole”.
          %p
            Now by the discussion at
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+bundle"} principal bundle
            = succeed "-principal" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cocycles"} cocycles
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cech+cohomology"} Cech cohomology
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 4
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^4
            with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coefficients"} coefficients
            in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            = succeed "-valued" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/good+open+cover"} good open cover
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 4
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^4
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/covering"} covering
            is already sufficient: we cover the
            = succeed "-sphere" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^n
            by two hemi-
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            \-spheres that overlap a bit at the equator, which is hence of the form
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo ×
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mi ϵ
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ϵ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^{n-1} \times [-\epsilon, \epsilon]
            = succeed "-valed" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo →
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^{n-1} \to G
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/clutching+construction"} clutching construction
          %p
            Moreover, a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+transformation"} gauge transformation
            of such a Cech cocycle is given by multiplying with the restriction of
            = succeed "-valued" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            = succeed "-spheres" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ≃
                  %msup
                    %mi D
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \simeq D^n
            to the equator. This just means that those transition functions
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 3
                  %mo →
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^3 \to G
            are gauge-trivial which may be extended smoothly to funtions
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi D
                      %mn 4
                    %mo →
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D^4 \to G
          %p
            In conclusion, the desired classification of instanton solutions by homotopy classes of maps
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 3
                  %mo →
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U \colon S^3 \to G
            is precisely the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/clutching+construction"} clutching construction
            of
            = succeed "-principal" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
          %p
            Finally, in order to add the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+connections"} principal connections
            to the picture, we think of one of the two semi-
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            \-spheres to be the neighbourhood of infinity and hence, since the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+strength"} field strength
            is demanded to be
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vanishing+at+infinity"} vanishing at infinity
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoid+of+Lie+algebra+valued+1-forms"} Lie algebra valued differential 1-form
            there. But then the rules for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cech+cohomology"} Cech cohomology
            with coefficients in the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoid+of+Lie+algebra+valued+1-forms"} groupoid of Lie algebra valued 1-forms
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/clutching+construction"} clutching construction
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi U
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %mi d
                    %mi U
                    %mo ∈
                    %msup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 3
                    %mo ×
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mi ϵ
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ϵ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U^{-1} d U \in \Omega^1( S^3 \times (-\epsilon, \epsilon) )
            = succeed "-sphere" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi D
                      %mn 4
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D^4
          %p
            Notice that this is precisely the argument which for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                  %mo =
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G = U(1)
            the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/circle+group"} circle group
            and for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                  %mo =
                  %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n = 2
            is known as the argument of
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dirac+charge+quantization"} Dirac charge quantization
            (which is also often misrepresented in the physics literature…)
          %p
            For more see at
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a{:href => "Yang-Mills+instanton#FromTheMathsToThePhysicsStory"} Yang-Mills instanton – SU(2)-instantons from the correct maths to the traditional physics story
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/interacting+vacuum"} interacting vacuum
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber+bundles+in+physics"} fiber bundles in physics
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/non-perturbative+effect"} non-perturbative effect
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yang-Mills+instanton"} Yang-Mills instanton
              %ul
                %li
                  %p
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/theta+vacuum"} theta vacuum
                %li
                  %p
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BPST-instanton"} BPST-instanton
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+tunneling"} quantum tunneling
            %li
              %p
                at
                = succeed ":" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/thermal+field+theory"} finite temperature
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/caloron"} caloron
              %ul
                %li
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/caloron+correspondence"} caloron correspondence
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CP+violation"} CP violation
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/baryogenesis"} baryogenesis
            %li
              %p
                %a{:href => "http://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/On+Vortex+Atoms#SimilarityToParticlePhysics"} vortex atoms – Similarity to concepts in modern particle physics
          %h2#References References
          %h3#general General
          %p
            (See also the general references at
            = succeed ".)" do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/instanton"} instanton
          %p Textbook account:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Robert+E.+Marshak"}> Robert E. Marshak
              , Section 10.3 of:
              = succeed "," do
                %em Conceptual Foundations of Modern Particle Physics
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1142/1767"} doi:10.1142/1767
          %p Physics-style surveys include the introductory lecture notes
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Marcos+Marino"}> Marcos Marino
                ,
                %em
                  Instantons and Large
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi N
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N
                  – An introduction to non-perturbative methods in QFT
                (
                %a{:href => "http://laces.web.cern.ch/laces/LACES10/notes/instlargen.pdf"}> pdf
                )
            %li#Forkel
              %p
                Hilmar Forkel,
                %em A Primer on Instantons in QCD
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-ph/0009136"}> arXiv:hep-ph/0009136
                )
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Edward+Shuryak"}> Edward Shuryak
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Physics of QCD Instantons
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.worldscientific.com/doi/abs/10.1142/9789812796653_0003"} web
          %p and the fairly detailed account (with lots of pointers to the literature)
          %ul
            %li#SchaeferShuryak98
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thomas+Schaefer"}> Thomas Schaefer
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Edward+Shuryak"} Edward Shuryak
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Instantons in QCD
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-ph/9610451"} arXiv:hep-ph/9610451
              %p#SchaeferShuryak
                section III D: relation to
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/confinement"} confinement
            %li
              %p
                Dmitri Diakonov,
                %em Instantons at work
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-ph/0212026"}> arXiv:hep-ph/0212026
                )
          %p See also the survey in
          %ul
            %li
              Marcus Hutter,
              %em Instantons in QCD: Theory and Application of the Instanton Liquid Model
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-ph/0107098"}> arXiv:hep-ph/0107098
              )
          %p
            On possible experimental signatures at the
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/LHC"} LHC
          %ul
            %li
              Simone Amoroso, Deepak Kar, Matthias Schott,
              %em How to discover QCD Instantons at the LHC
              (
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2012.09120"}> arXiv:2012.09120
              )
          %p
            Detailed argument for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/theta-vacuum"} theta-vacuum
            structure from
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chiral+symmetry+breaking"} chiral symmetry breaking
            is offered in
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Curtis+Callan"}> Curtis Callan
                , R.F. Dashen,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/David+Gross"} David Gross
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The Structure of the Gauge Theory Vacuum
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://inspirehep.net/record/3673?ln=en"} spire
            %li
              %p
                G. Morchio,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Franco+Strocchi"} Franco Strocchi
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Chiral symmetry breaking and theta vacuum structure in QCD
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/0907.2522"} arXiv:0907.2522
          %p
            A review in view of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/asymptotic+series"} asymptotic series
            nature of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Feynman+perturbation+series"} Feynman perturbation series
            is in
          %ul
            %li#Suslov05
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Igor+Suslov"}> Igor Suslov
              , section 4.5 of
              = succeed "," do
                %em Divergent perturbation series
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-ph/0510142"} arXiv:hep-ph/0510142
          %p
            A survey with emphasis on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strong+CP+problem"} strong CP problem
            is in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Roberto+Peccei"}> Roberto Peccei
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em The Strong CP Problem and Axions
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-ph/0607268"} arXiv:hep-ph/0607268
          %p
            A more mathematically precise account which identifies instanton solutions explicitly equivalence classes of
            = succeed "-principal" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
          %ul
            %li#Nakahara
              Nakahara,
              %em Geometry Topology and Physics
          %p This perspective is for instance also the one used in
          %ul#Witten85
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Edward+Witten"}> Edward Witten
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Global gravitational anomalies
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://projecteuclid.org/euclid.cmp/1103943444"} Euclid
          %p
            Discussion in the context of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chiral+symmetry+breaking"} chiral symmetry breaking
            includes
          %ul
            %li#Diakonov96
              Dmitri Diakonov,
              %em Chiral Symmetry Breaking by Instantons
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-ph/9602375"}> arXiv:hep-ph/9602375
              )
          %p
            Discussion in the context of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/confinement"} confinement
            includes
          %ul
            %li
              Y. M. Cho,
              %em Dimensional Transmutation by Monopole Condensation in QCD
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1206.6936"}> arXiv:1206.6936
              )
          %p
            Discussion in the context of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quark-gluon+plasma"} quark-gluon plasma
            includes
          %ul
            %li#Shuryak01
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Edward+Shuryak"}> Edward Shuryak
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Nonperturbative QCD and Quark-Gluon Plasma
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://users.ictp.it/~pub_off/lectures/lns010/Shuryak/Shuryak.pdf"} pdf
            %li
              %p
                Nikolai Kochelev,
                %em Ultra-light Glueballs in Quark-Gluon Plasma
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1501.07002"}> arXiv:1501.07002
                )
          %p Discussion of the infrared problem of the QCD instanton vacuum model includes
          %ul
            %li#Witten98
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Edward+Witten"}> Edward Witten
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Theta Dependence In The Large N Limit Of Four-Dimensional Gauge Theories
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9807109"} arXiv:hep-th/9807109
          %p
            Discussion of instantons in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lattice+gauge+theory"} lattice gauge theory
            includes
          %ul
            %li#Moore03
              %p
                Guy Moore, section 7 of
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Informal lectures on lattice gauge theory
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.physics.mcgill.ca/~guymoore/latt_lectures.pdf"} pdf
            %li#Creutz11
              %p
                Michael Creutz,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Anomalies, gauge field topology, and the lattice
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://thy.phy.bnl.gov/~creutz/mypubs/pub192.pdf"} pdf
            %li#Gruber13
              %p
                Florian Gruber,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Topology in dynamical Lattice QCD simulations
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://epub.uni-regensburg.de/27631/"} web
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://epub.uni-regensburg.de/27631/1/dissertation.pdf"} pdf
          %p
            and via the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+theory"} homotopy theory
            of
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bundle+gerbes"} bundle gerbes
          %ul
            %li
              Jing-Yuan Chen,
              %em Instanton Density Operator in Lattice QCD from Higher Category Theory
              \&amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2406.06673"}> arXiv:2406.06673
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            Discussion of the
            = succeed "-mass" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi η
                    %mo ′
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta'
          %ul
            %li#Witten79
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Edward+Witten"}> Edward Witten
                , Nucl. Phys. B 156 (1979) 269.
            %li#Veneziano79
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gabriele+Veneziano"}> Gabriele Veneziano
                , Nucl. Phys. B 159 (1979) 213
            %li#Schaefer02
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thomas+Schaefer"}> Thomas Schaefer
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em QCD and the eta prime Mass: Instantons or Confinement?
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-lat/0211035"} arXiv:hep-lat/0211035
            %li
              %p
                %em
                  A renewed look at
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi η
                        %mo ′
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta'
                  in medium, (
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1203.6740"}> arXiv:1203.6740
                  )
          %p
            Relation to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/scanning+map"} scanning map
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/configuration+spaces+of+points"} configuration spaces of points
            in:
          %ul
            %li#AtiyahJones78
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Atiyah"}> Michael Atiyah
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+David+Stuart+Jones"} John David Stuart Jones
              = succeed "," do
                %em Topological aspects of Yang-Mills theory
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://projecteuclid.org/euclid.cmp/1103904210"} arXiv:1103904210
          %h3#relation_to_skyrmions_calorons_monopoles Relation to skyrmions, calorons, monopoles
          %p
            The construction of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Skyrmions"} Skyrmions
            from
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/instantons"} instantons
            is due to
          %ul
            %li#AtiyahManton89
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Atiyah"}> Michael Atiyah
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %span.newWikiWord
                  Nicholar S. Manton
                  %a{:href => "/nlab/new/Nicholar+S.+Manton"} ?
              = succeed "," do
                %em Skyrmions from instantons
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/0370-2693(89)90340-7"} doi:10.1016/0370-2693(89)90340-7
          %p
            The relation between
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/skyrmions"} skyrmions
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/instantons"} instantons
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/calorons"} calorons
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/solitons"} solitons
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monopoles"} monopoles
            is usefully reviewed and further developed in
          %ul
            %li#Cork18a
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Josh+Cork"}> Josh Cork
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Calorons, symmetry, and the soliton trinity
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://etheses.whiterose.ac.uk/22097/"} web
            %li#Cork18b
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Josh+Cork"}> Josh Cork
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Skyrmions from calorons
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1810.04143"} arXiv:1810.04143
        .revisedby
